2 System build-up

2.1 The external wall build-up from inside to outside is:
12.5 mm plasterboard on 15 mm fire-rated board (by the drylining package);
150 mm SFS studs at 600 mm centres with 100 mm mineral wool between studs;
12 mm cement particle sheathing board;
vapour-permeable breather membrane, class A2-s1,d0;
160 mm Thermarock FS35 rainscreen insulation slab, mechanically fixed;
40 mm minimum ventilated cavity;
aluminium helping-hand brackets and vertical T and L rails;
brick slip carrier panels with 20 mm clay brick slips, colour Eastbrook Buff, pointed in mortar colour Natural.

2.2 The calculated U-value of the typical wall build-up is 0.16 W/m²K, including bracket bridging factors.

2.3 Brackets shall be fixed to the slab edges at every floor. Fixings into slab edges shall maintain a minimum edge distance of 100 mm. Where cast-in channels are provided in the slab edge, brackets shall be fixed to the channels using the channel manufacturer's T-bolts.

2.4 Movement joints. Vertical movement joints shall be provided at a maximum of 6 m centres and at all internal corners. Horizontal movement joints shall be provided at every floor level to accommodate slab deflection and frame shortening.

2.5 Pointing. Brick slip joints shall be 10 mm, struck flush, using the panel manufacturer's factory-matched mortar. The final mortar colour shall be confirmed on the mock-up.

Eastbrook Building Control – Site Inspection Record
Reference: ALD-INS-BC-005. Site: Aldermoor Court, 14 Aldermoor Road, Eastbrook. Inspection date: Tuesday 22 September 2026. Inspector: Rui Tanaka, Building Control Surveyor. Met on site by Dana Whitlock (Halvern Build Ltd).

Stage inspected: basement car park and plant room – fire safety, ventilation and drainage, before ceiling services are closed in.

Items inspected:
Car park jet fan ventilation installation (6 jet fans, 2 extract fans);
Sprinkler installation in the car park, including the valve set in the plant room;
Fire-stopping of service penetrations through the plant room and cycle store enclosure walls;
Slot drains and petrol interceptor access covers;
Protected lobbies to cores A and B at basement level.

Defect D1 (must be resolved): Three service penetrations (two cable trays and one 110 mm drainage pipe) through the 120-minute plant room wall into the car park are not fire-stopped. The penetrations must be sealed with a tested fire-stopping system appropriate to the service and the wall, and labelled. This defect must be closed before the next inspection.

Observation O1: Jet fan JF-03 is mounted 300 mm from a sprinkler head; confirm with the sprinkler designer that the discharge pattern is not obstructed.

Observation O2: The commissioning certificates for the car park ventilation, including the CO and NO2 detection set points, must be provided before the completion inspection.
